# IMG on the manual's Cassegrain (cmdref: Outputs).  Without an ObjFile= the command refuses ("Object
# intensity input not available"); the deck is then given ObjFile= obj.txt, a 256 x 256 (the model's
# diffraction grid) 0/1 map with an 8 x 8 square at its center, written by awk beside the deck.  IMG
# prompts for the element and must be at the focal plane (3 refuses: "Imaging must be on focal plane!").
# Incoherent: the image is the PSF convolved with the object -- its sum 2.1204e10 is the PSF's 3.3131e8
# times the 64 object pixels, peak 2.24e8 at (128,128).  Coherent (fixed 2026-10-18, PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2
# (s)): SysImging divided the amplitude convolution by size**2 and then overwrote it, so the coherent image
# was size**4 = 4.3e9 too bright (peak 5.3e19, sum 2.2e21 before).  Now the textbook checks: a POINT object
# (one pixel, pt.txt) images to the PSF itself in both modes -- the same peak and the PSF's sum 3.3131e8 --
# and the square's coherent flux is 24.7 x its incoherent flux, inside Cauchy-Schwarz's [1, 64] for 64
# in-phase unit emitters.  The TEXT plot type writes each image to Cassegrain.in.intensity5.txt.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
cd $TMP
old $DECK
none
int 5
img
! awk 'BEGIN{for(i=1;i<=256;i++){for(j=1;j<=256;j++)printf "%d ",(i>124&&i<133&&j>124&&j<133);print ""}}' > obj.txt
! perl -i -pe 'print "ObjFile= obj.txt\n" if $. == 1' $DECK
old $DECK
none
int 5
img
3
text
img
5
inc
! awk '{for(j=1;j<=NF;j++){s+=$j;if($j>m){m=$j;r=NR;c=j}}}END{print "IMG",r,c,m,s}' Cassegrain.in.intensity5.txt
! cp Cassegrain.in.intensity5.txt inc_square.txt
img
5
coh
yes
! awk '{for(j=1;j<=NF;j++){s+=$j;if($j>m){m=$j;r=NR;c=j}}}END{print "IMG",r,c,m,s}' Cassegrain.in.intensity5.txt
! awk 'FNR==NR{for(j=1;j<=NF;j++)a+=$j;next}{for(j=1;j<=NF;j++)b+=$j}END{r=b/a;print "RATIO",r,(r>=1&&r<=64)?"inbound":"OUT"}' inc_square.txt Cassegrain.in.intensity5.txt
! awk 'BEGIN{for(i=1;i<=256;i++){for(j=1;j<=256;j++)printf "%d ",(i==129&&j==129);print ""}}' > pt.txt
! perl -i -pe 's/^ObjFile= obj.txt/ObjFile= pt.txt/' $DECK
old $DECK
none
text
int 5
img
5
inc
yes
! awk '{for(j=1;j<=NF;j++){s+=$j;if($j>m){m=$j;r=NR;c=j}}}END{print "PT",r,c,m,s}' Cassegrain.in.intensity5.txt
img
5
coh
yes
! awk '{for(j=1;j<=NF;j++){s+=$j;if($j>m){m=$j;r=NR;c=j}}}END{print "PT",r,c,m,s}' Cassegrain.in.intensity5.txt
# EXPECT: MACOS> img\s+\* Object intensity input not available
# EXPECT: Enter number of element where data is to be generated: \[5\]: 3[\s\S]*?Geometric Prop between Elt  0 and Elt  3 to WF  1[\s\S]*?Imaging must be on focal plane!
# EXPECT: INCoherent or COHerent imaging\? \[INC\]: inc[\s\S]*?- End of incoherent imaging\s+Writing Incoherent Imaging, Elt=5
# EXPECT: Text array is of dimension   256 by   256\. Magnitude of central pixel is  0\.22413\d+D\+09
# EXPECT: IMG 128 128 2\.2413\d+E\+08 2\.120\d+e\+10
# EXPECT: INCoherent or COHerent imaging\? \[INC\]: coh[\s\S]*?- End of coherent imaging
# EXPECT: Writing Coherent Imaging, Elt=5
# EXPECT: IMG 128 128 1\.23291\d+E\+10 5\.235\d+e\+11
# EXPECT: ^RATIO 24\.\d+ inbound\s*$
# EXPECT: Sum of intensity= 3\.3131\d*D\+08
# EXPECT: ^PT (128 129 8\.8773\d*E\+06 3\.3131\d*e\+08)\s*$[\s\S]*?^PT \1\s*$
# EXPECT-NOT: RATIO \S+ OUT
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
